<!--Render Target Documentation — DomainBoundary
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.DomainBoundary-->
<rdoc:DomainBoundary xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    What this target reads from @machineblocks/core
  </is>
  <documentation>
    This package depends on @machineblocks/core and does not copy its blocks.

    Read there:

    - com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.ScadRenderTarget — orientation
    - com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.MbBlockApi — mb_block signature
    - com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.BlockFileStructure — file sections
      as the library presents them
    - com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.TypesAndSerialization — short
      serialization sketch; SerializationRules in this library is the compiler
      emit contract when the two differ, and type BML wins for shapes
    - com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.ModulePatterns
    - com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.ScadDecisionRules
    - com.machineblocks.bml.core.NativeBlock — parameter inventory
    - com.machineblocks.bml.type.* — type shapes
    - com.machineblocks.bml.examples.* — example BML
    - blocks/com/machineblocks/scad/** — corresponding SCAD, including
      examples/Cross.scad and examples/Connector.scad
    - lib/block.scad and config/mb_config.scad — runtime imports

    Do not move those files into this package. When an example .scad and this
    target's emit rules diverge, the BML example plus this library are the
    intended compiler output; hand-maintained SCAD may still show the older
    wrapper style that LeafOptimization removes.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Introduction" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</rdoc:DomainBoundary>
